**Drawing to make (large, in pencil, with ruled label lines):** a single cell of *Spirogyra* taken from a filament, drawn as a rectangle about twice as long as wide, with:

- a thin **cell wall** forming the outline (cellulose);
- the **cell membrane** just inside the wall (drawn as a thin line against it);
- a thin layer of **cytoplasm** lining the wall;
- one or two **spiral (ribbon-like) chloroplasts** running in a helix along the cell, drawn as a wavy band;
- small round **pyrenoids** embedded in the chloroplast (dots on the ribbon);
- a large **central vacuole** containing cell sap, filling the middle of the cell;
- a **nucleus** in the middle of the cell, suspended by thin **cytoplasmic strands** across the vacuole.

Give the drawing a title (*A cell of Spirogyra*) and label at least six parts.
